{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-164397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-4)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =1 \\\\ 8-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7} & =7 \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =49 \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm 7 \\\\ y & =-1\\pm 7 \\\\ y & =-8,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=-8$ and $y=6$ in the $yz$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "56044477bfe4e219edf038aecd64b41c38a2cd330e13447acc9eef3404bcca5a"} {"question" "q-164397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The ellipse $\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}=1$"] ["text" "The hyperbola $\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{7}-{z}^{2}=1$"] ["text" "The line $y=-1$"] ["text" "The line $y=6$"] ["text" "The lines $y=-8$ and $y=6$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The lines $y=-8$ and $y=6$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{2}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-4 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =4\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $x=2$ and $x=6$ in the $xz$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "56044477bfe4e219edf038aecd64b41c38a2cd330e13447acc9eef3404bcca5a"} {"question" "q-164401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The ellipse $\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}=1$"] ["text" "The hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{2}=1$"] ["text" "The line $x=4$"] ["text" "The line $x=6$"] ["text" "The lines $x=2$ and $x=6$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The lines $x=2$ and $x=6$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The projection of the intersection between the parabolic cylinder $4(x-3)^{2}=12(z+1)$ and the plane $y=2$ onto the $xz$-plane is a parabola. What is the vertex of the parabola?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $y=2,$ we substitute $y=2$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $y$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-3)^{2} & =12(z+1) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =3(z+1) \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =4\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (z+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a parabola in the $xz$-plane with the vertex at $(3,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "56044477bfe4e219edf038aecd64b41c38a2cd330e13447acc9eef3404bcca5a"} {"question" "q-164414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-3,1)"] ["math" "(2,-1)"] ["math" "(3,-1)"] ["math" "(3,1)"] ["math" "(3,2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3,-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The full expression describing all points on our hyperbolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola centered at $(0,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "56044477bfe4e219edf038aecd64b41c38a2cd330e13447acc9eef3404bcca5a"} {"question" "q-164416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }x-y>12}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(0,-1)$"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(0,1)$"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(1,0)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperbola centered at $(0,-1)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $(x-3)^{2}-\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{8}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The full expression describing all points on our hyperbolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x-3)^{2}-\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{8}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }(x-3)^{2}-\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{8}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola centered at $(3,-6).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "56044477bfe4e219edf038aecd64b41c38a2cd330e13447acc9eef3404bcca5a"} {"question" "q-164418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:x\\ge 3}"] ["math" "{R}^{2}"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(-3,6)$"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(1,2\\sqrt{2})$"] ["text" "A hyperbola centered at $(3,-6)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"} {"question" "q-164418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperbola centered at $(3,-6)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072950/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f13dd91ded0b9b85e8cb1e7d03e6eed7934c692f41d37c15036220510aa4723"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2675 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
